	(text "BUS ENTRY + FUSING\nF101 protects everything downstream. It is NOT the over-current\nprotection - that is the ±45 A comparator on each power_channel.\nThis clears shorted-FET and shorted-bus faults, where current is\nlimited only by battery impedance.\n70 A: bus draw is coil current × duty ≈ 30 A average per board with\n60 A peaks. MIDI HP series is 70 VDC rated; most automotive fuses\nare 32 V and would be wrong here."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 69.088 64.516 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2c2caca5-29b5-40c9-8b6f-6a1a90c9efab")
	)
	(text "BULK ENERGY STORAGE\n6 × 470 µF, shared by both power_channel instances. Sized by RIPPLE\nCURRENT, not capacitance: ~20 A RMS on the shared bus once the two\nchannels are interleaved 180°. Select parts so the ripple ratings\nsum past 20 A - the count follows the part.\nR101 bleeds 5.1 J of stored energy: under 10 V in ~110 s."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 114.046 102.362 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "5cf310a2-d526-4782-b649-109a686c0fb1")
	)
